{"id":"consistently-slower","title":"Consistently slower: who the process holds up","question":"Which firms and licensed professionals wait longer than like permits, year after year?","finding":"93 of 1,157 firms and professionals tested are consistently slower than like permits, where chance alone would produce about 0.05; 63 still stand out after also matching the kind of work. Slowest after the control: Jim Parr dba Plumbing, faster on only 7% of 142 jobs (2012–2023), a median 30 days against 0 for like permits. 4 further individuals are counted, not named.","how":"Every issued building permit with drawings filed 2012 to 2024 (179,746 permits) was ranked by days from filing to issue among like permits: the same permit type, review path (counter or full review, Fire-only, site permit, online filing, and the department's own priority flag), cost band and filing year. Cells under 30 permits were merged upward (three-year period, then paired cost bands) and 388 permits with no cell of 30 were dropped. A job is faster when it beat its cell's median; ties at the median are split in proportion so that chance gives exactly one half. Firms are tested with 40 or more jobs and at least 3 active years (5 or more jobs in the year); jobs for one lot filed on one day count once. Contractors are joined on their State licence number, other firms on the exact normalised name. With 1,157 firms tested, the usual one-in-twenty threshold would pass about 58 by luck alone, so the cut is set at 4.1 standard errors, where about 0.05 firms in the whole list would pass by luck. As a check on the arithmetic, the same permits dealt at random into 1,199 pretend firms put 5.8% beyond the usual threshold and 0 beyond the strict cut. Consistent means beyond that cut, on the same side of one half in at least three quarters of active years, and at least 55% (or at most 45%) overall. The last two columns repeat the comparison inside cells that also match the kind of work (keywords in the permit description) and the building's use.","limits":"A firm can be slow for honest reasons too: work that needs Planning review or neighbor notice inside an ordinary-looking permit type (antennas, changes of use), clients who pay fees late (a permit is issued only when its fees are paid), drawings that need rounds of correction, or a habit of filing early and collecting the permit later. Where the difference does not survive the kind-of-work control it is most likely the kind of work. The records do not say whether a wait was the City's or the applicant's. Names typed differently on different permits are counted as different firms.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"firm","t":"Firm or licensed professional","type":"org"},{"k":"role","t":"Listed on permits as","type":"text"},{"k":"jobs","t":"Jobs compared","type":"int"},{"k":"years","t":"Active years","type":"text"},{"k":"yearsWith","t":"Years slower than half","type":"text"},{"k":"share","t":"Share faster than the like-permit median","type":"pct"},{"k":"days","t":"Their median days to issue","type":"days"},{"k":"like","t":"Median for like permits","type":"days"},{"k":"value","t":"Construction value on those permits","type":"usd"},{"k":"workShare","t":"Share faster after also matching the kind of work","type":"pct"},{"k":"survives","t":"Difference survives that control?","type":"text"},{"k":"premium","t":"Share of their jobs flagged 'Premium'","type":"pct"},{"k":"mostly","t":"Most common kind of work","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"firm":"Jim Parr dba Plumbing","firmKey":null,"role":"Contractor","jobs":142,"years":"2012–2023","yearsWith":"10 of 10","share":0.074,"days":29.5,"like":0.0,"value":2171652,"workShare":0.08,"survives":"Yes","premium":0.0,"mostly":"fire sprinklers (55%)"},{"firm":"C & E Electric & Fire Alarm Services","firmKey":null,"role":"Contractor","jobs":110,"years":"2021–2024","yearsWith":"3 of 4","share":0.107,"days":117.5,"like":0.0,"value":3821877,"workShare":0.099,"survives":"Yes","premium":0.0,"mostly":"fire a